eIdentifier":"s:SZ","text":"SignedInteger","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A positive supply is how much more the vertex sends than it receives; a negative one is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"demand. There is no flow when the supplies do not sum to zero or some set of vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"supplies more than its out-edges carry. Costs may be negative, and negative cycles are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"saturated. A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise. Capacities may be of an unsigned type, up to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int.max","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Computed by the network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Which optimum is returned when several exist is unspecified, but the same input always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives the same result. ","type":"text"},{"code":"supply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, then, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each edge in position order, ","type":"text"},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and then ","type":"text"},{"code":"cost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", before any work.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every capacity is at least zero; capacities, supplies and costs fit in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; Σ capacity × |cost| fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Cost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (checked before solving, since it bounds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"total cost); 4(n + 1)(the greatest |cost| of a non-loop edge + 1) fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solver’s artificial cost, with room for its potentials and reduced costs); the positive","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"supplies sum within ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note"}]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols":{"title":"GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/flows","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"Flows"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertex":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","title":"Vertex","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertex","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"title":"DirectedGraph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flow